 "cues": [
  {
   "s": 1,
   "e": 3.44,
   "text": "Announcing Aomi Task API."
  },
  {
   "s": 6.49,
   "e": 8.168,
   "text": "Here's a treasury agent on Arc"
  },
  {
   "s": 8.208,
   "e": 9.945,
   "text": "sending one long instruction:"
  },
  {
   "s": 9.985,
   "e": 14.159,
   "text": "rebalance into EURC, JPYC and MXNB,"
  },
  {
   "s": 14.199,
   "e": 19.697,
   "text": "fill within 15 bps of mid, keep 25,000 USDC for payroll,"
  },
  {
   "s": 19.737,
   "e": 22.769,
   "text": "and revert everything if any leg fails."
  },
  {
   "s": 25.019,
   "e": 28.114,
   "text": "Aomi's harness turns that into transactions"
  },
  {
   "s": 28.154,
   "e": 30.203,
   "text": "across StableFX and Arc pools,"
  },
  {
   "s": 30.243,
   "e": 32.491,
   "text": "so the agent never writes calldata."
  },
  {
   "s": 32.531,
   "e": 35.834,
   "text": "Then it runs the whole batch on an internal fork of Arc,"
  },
  {
   "s": 35.874,
   "e": 39.255,
   "text": "and checks every constraint against the result."
  },
  {
   "s": 40.505,
   "e": 42.566,
   "text": "What comes back is an outcome fingerprint,"
  },
  {
   "s": 42.606,
   "e": 48.964,
   "text": "signed by Aomi: 22,000 USDC out, EURC and JPYC in,"
  },
  {
   "s": 49.004,
   "e": 52.853,
   "text": "every constraint passed, and the MXNB leg skipped,"
  },
  {
   "s": 52.893,
   "e": 56.301,
   "text": "because the best fill was 19 bps from mid."
  },
  {
   "s": 56.341,
   "e": 58.576,
   "text": "Getting this far costs one cent."
  },
  {
   "s": 58.616,
   "e": 60.155,
   "text": "The buyer sees the outcome before"
  },
  {
   "s": 60.195,
   "e": 62.17,
   "text": "anything touches its wallet."
  },
  {
   "s": 64.021,
   "e": 65.2,
   "text": "Now the buyer decides."
  },
  {
   "s": 65.24,
   "e": 66.233,
   "text": "If it wants the batch,"
  },
  {
   "s": 66.273,
   "e": 69.6,
   "text": "it pays 3% of the USDC leaving its wallet,"
  },
  {
   "s": 69.64,
   "e": 75.842,
   "text": "here 660 USDC, over x402, and gets the full bundle."
  },
  {
   "s": 78.692,
   "e": 81.891,
   "text": "Then it signs and broadcasts the bundle itself."
  },
  {
   "s": 81.931,
   "e": 84.84,
   "text": "Aomi never holds its keys or its funds."
  },
  {
   "s": 84.88,
   "e": 87.023,
   "text": "What Aomi sells is the work:"
  },
  {
   "s": 87.063,
   "e": 90.842,
   "text": "a harness that runs complex money-lego intents faster,"
  },
  {
   "s": 90.882,
   "e": 93.949,
   "text": "more reliably, and with fewer tokens."
  },
  {
   "s": 94.799,
   "e": 97.011,
   "text": "Watch a real run on Arc Mainnet."
  },
  {
   "s": 97.051,
   "e": 98.764,
   "text": "The agent asks to send 0.1 and"
  },
  {
   "s": 98.804,
   "e": 101.702,
   "text": "0.2 USDC to two ops wallets,"
  },
  {
   "s": 101.742,
   "e": 105.696,
   "text": "and pays one cent over x402 to prepare."
  },
  {
   "s": 105.736,
   "e": 109.191,
   "text": "It polls for free until the simulation passes every check."
  },
  {
   "s": 109.231,
   "e": 112.348,
   "text": "Retrieval costs 3% of the thirty cents moved,"
  },
  {
   "s": 112.388,
   "e": 114.961,
   "text": "so 0.009 USDC."
  },
  {
   "s": 115.001,
   "e": 118.618,
   "text": "Then its own wallet signs, both transfers confirm onchain,"
  },
  {
   "s": 118.658,
   "e": 121.202,
   "text": "and the recipient balances are verified."
  },
  {
   "s": 122.052,
   "e": 123.382,
   "text": "Why does this matter?"
  },
  {
   "s": 123.422,
   "e": 126.656,
   "text": "x402 already lets agents pay for data."
  },
  {
   "s": 126.696,
   "e": 129.28,
   "text": "The chain sits in between as a neutral rail,"
  },
  {
   "s": 129.32,
   "e": 131.876,
   "text": "so neither side has to trust the other."
  },
  {
   "s": 132.426,
   "e": 134.743,
   "text": "But what if an agent wants to buy a service?"
  },
  {
   "s": 134.783,
   "e": 136.438,
   "text": "The outcome of the work cannot"
  },
  {
   "s": 136.478,
   "e": 139.185,
   "text": "be pre-verified before delivery."
  },
  {
   "s": 140.635,
   "e": 142.162,
   "text": "People haven't solved this either."
  },
  {
   "s": 142.202,
   "e": 143.904,
   "text": "You cannot tell whether a contractor"
  },
  {
   "s": 143.944,
   "e": 146.558,
   "text": "does good jobs before seeing them work."
  },
  {
   "s": 148.208,
   "e": 151.036,
   "text": "This loop never completes in the human economy."
  },
  {
   "s": 151.076,
   "e": 152.162,
   "text": "Machines can do better,"
  },
  {
   "s": 152.202,
   "e": 153.915,
   "text": "because their service is usually"
  },
  {
   "s": 153.955,
   "e": 156.04,
   "text": "the result of processing data,"
  },
  {
   "s": 156.08,
   "e": 158.508,
   "text": "which can be checked before it's delivered."
  },
  {
   "s": 159.263,
   "e": 161.034,
   "text": "A transparent settlement layer,"
  },
  {
   "s": 161.074,
   "e": 164.32,
   "text": "plus machine work that can be checked before delivery,"
  },
  {
   "s": 164.36,
   "e": 168.065,
   "text": "makes outcome-based pricing for services possible."
  },
  {
   "s": 169.115,
   "e": 171.641,
   "text": "One trust assumption remains: today,"
  },
  {
   "s": 171.681,
   "e": 175.565,
   "text": "the buyer trusts that Aomi's simulation ran honestly."
  },
  {
   "s": 175.605,
   "e": 177.69,
   "text": "Next, we plan to run the harness in"
  },
  {
   "s": 177.73,
   "e": 179.907,
   "text": "a trusted execution environment,"
  },
  {
   "s": 179.947,
   "e": 182.84,
   "text": "so buying a service becomes trustless."
  },
  {
   "s": 184.89,
   "e": 188.519,
   "text": "The Task API is live, settling in USDC on Arc."
  },
  {
   "s": 188.559,
   "e": 191.045,
   "text": "Try it at aomi.dev."
  }
 ],
